The firststarts is a list of 0, 5, 13, and 24.
The firstends is a list of 2, 10, 23, and 25.
The secondstarts is a list of 1, 8, 15, and 25.
The secondends is a list of 5, 12, 24, and 26.
The first is 0.
The second is 0.
The found is 0.
Repeat while first is at most the last position of firststarts and second is at most the last position of secondstarts.
The low is item first of firststarts.
If item second of secondstarts is more than low, set low to item second of secondstarts.
The high is item first of firstends.
If item second of secondends is less than high, set high to item second of secondends.
The firstend is item first of firstends.
The secondend is item second of secondends.
If firstend is less than secondend, add 1 to first, otherwise add 1 to second.
If low is at most high.
If found is more than 0, show "---".
Show low.
Show high.
Add 1 to found.
